Package: prescco
Type: Package
Title: Semiparametric Prediction Intervals Under a Censored Covariate
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kihyun", "Han", email = "kqh5716@psu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Constructs prediction intervals for an outcome when a
    time-to-event covariate is subject to right-censoring. The package provides
    a general, data-in toolkit that operates on supplied data with optional
    fully-observed covariates (continuous and discrete): maximum-likelihood
    estimation of the working X | Z and C | Z models, two coefficient
    estimators (complete-case least squares and the semiparametric-efficient
    SPARCC estimator), and two families of prediction intervals
    (semiparametric and conformal: split, full, and jackknife+). A separate,
    self-contained, no-covariate simulation study ships alongside the package
    under 'sim/' and is run by sourcing 'sim/run.R' (it is not part of the
    installed package namespace). The name abbreviates PREdiction with
    Semiparametric Efficiency under a right-Censored COvariate.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    MASS,
    truncnorm,
